.TH APER-SEARCH 1 "July 28, 2026" "aper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aper-search \- search a bounded substitution space and render its survivor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aper-search
.RB [ \-c " scheme" ]
.RB [ \-n " depth" ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-k | \-\-classify }
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-l | \-\-list-known }
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-h | \-\-help }
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-V | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aper-search
exercises the discovery pipeline over one deliberately small control problem:
covering a unit square with half-scale squares on a 2 by 2 grid.
It enumerates the exact cover, checks its substitution matrix and geometry,
verifies five generations, removes canonically equivalent results, and writes
the surviving rule or patch as native vector PDF to standard output.
.PP
The discovered square grid is periodic.  It is a control case for extending
the search to richer prototiles, not a claim of novelty or aperiodicity.
.PP
The known-rule bank contains the Encyclopedia systems independently encoded
by aper.  Classification tests exact canonical rule equivalence only.  Failure
to match this necessarily incomplete bank is not evidence of novelty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-colour " " scheme
Select
.BR flare ,
.BR grove ,
.BR electric ,
or
.BR tide .
The default is
.BR flare .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-depth " " depth
Render the patch after 1 through 7 substitutions.
The default is 4.
This option may not be used with rule output.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rule
Render the discovered substitution rule instead of a finite patch.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-classify
Write a text classification of the survivor against the encoded known-rule
bank instead of rendering PDF.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list-known
List the local system id, Encyclopedia record, and source URL for every
encoded known rule.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a concise help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the control search and render its depth-4 patch:
.PP
.EX
aper-search > square-candidate.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render the rule found by the same search:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --rule > square-rule.pdf
.EE
.PP
Inspect the executable bank and classify the square control:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --list-known
aper-search --classify
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/aper/encyclopedia.tsv
Metadata-only reference index of the Tilings Encyclopedia substitution pages.
Installed separately by
.BR "make install-encyclopedia" .
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/aper/encyclopedia.NOTICE.md
Attribution, licence, and transformation notice for the reference index.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B aper-search
exits zero after writing the requested PDF, classification, or bank listing.
It exits non-zero if its arguments are invalid, the search invariant fails,
or output cannot be written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aper (1)
